{"kind":"assert","text":"Draft 2 of the client design note answers review eef4c7ba.\nBranch `planner/client-primitive-note-20261113`, commit 9afd311b,\nfile `notes/2026-11-13-scope-client.md`. Hugh ratifies it.\n\nYour points, by number:\n1. Section 6 is now six ordered rules, and the first that holds\n   gives the status. An acceptance or a `mismatch` that the\n   replica is behind reads `pending`. Invariant 2 of section 12\n   checks one status and one place for each key.\n2. Section 3 defines an attempt. Only an answer to a copy of the\n   current attempt returns a request. The client ends a send at\n   30 s and reads no later reply.\n3. Rule 5 builds the intent at the replica's head at each submit.\n   It sends old bytes only when a live signing equals the built\n   intent apart from `notAfter`. The answer `expired` makes a\n   signing dead. A meaning excludes `expected` and `notAfter`.\n4. Submit signs and keeps before the draft counts as taken. The\n   draft store takes no write at a submit. The draft state\n   `submitting` covers the click to the kept signing. A stop has\n   the causes `shape`, `state`, `busy`, `signer`, `store`, `full`\n   and `taken`. The suite reloads between signing and write.\n5. A draft lives from the first edit to a discard or the end of\n   its request, whatever its values. `restore` needs an empty\n   slot, so nothing is exchanged. Section 8 states when a request\n   leaves the list. Section 9 defines `DraftView` and `ItemRef`.\n6. Section 3 defines a closed signing. Custody keeps an envelope\n   until its signing is closed. The false paragraph is gone.\n7. Invariant 1 counts intentions from the member's steps. The\n   suite has two clocks.\n8. A slot follows from the step, the `on` item and each `item`\n   field. Admission reads the `expected` items of the built\n   intent.\n9. The third case of section 2 is an edit that returns\n   `revision-moved`. The fourth uses `type-full`.\n10. C2 needs PG-1. `stopped` carries one of six causes. A kept\n   replica waits for 4893fbfa. A scope with an archive floor stops\n   the client. `folded` with a foreign intent gives `mismatch`. A\n   second tab reads `taken` or sends the kept bytes.\n\nOne ruling goes past your review. `withdrawn` needs a copy in\nflight that the judge admits at the replica's head. A returned\nedit with an old revision therefore reads `refused`.\n\nSection 14 lists the four choices that a member sees, for Hugh.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}